---
description: Astro, TypeScript, CSS and maintainability conventions
globs: "**/*.{astro,ts,tsx,js,mjs,css}"
alwaysApply: false
---

Follow `AGENTS.md`.

- Prefer clear, readable code over clever abstractions.
- Use semantic HTML and meaningful names.
- Keep Astro frontmatter concise; extract repeated UI into components only when useful.
- Avoid inline styles for new reusable patterns when a class would be clearer; do not refactor unrelated existing styles.
- Preserve established CSS selectors and page behaviour.
- Format modified files using project Prettier configuration with `prettier-plugin-astro`.
- Do not reformat unrelated files or add dependencies without a reason.
- Avoid `any` where practical; use types for nontrivial data.
- Ensure form handlers handle pending, success and error states without duplicate submissions.
